# FUNC + `nudge` takes stock's coarse steps (NOT: octaves) and comes back. The runner spends
# stock's dropped first FUNC turn itself. Coarse steps snap to stock's grid, so the value only
# returns when it began on the grid (NOT at a whole octave, as a new trig page has it).
name: link-func-nudge
state: changes

# TRIG pressed on its own page shows its second page, and the unit keeps that choice: come from another.
key AMP
key TRIG
wait 3500
screen rest
hold FUNC
nudge A +1
release FUNC
wait 3500
screen up
expect up != rest
hold FUNC
nudge A -1
nudge A -1
nudge A +1
release FUNC
wait 3500
screen back
expect back == rest
